3.3 Building the space-time panels构建时空面板


Code
make_panel &lt;- function(d, time_col, periods) {
  d |&gt;
    st_drop_geometry() |&gt;
    group_by(TS_PCODE, period = .data[[time_col]]) |&gt;
    summarise(conflict = n(),
              battles  = sum(event_type == "Battles"),
              erv      = sum(event_type == "Explosions/Remote violence"),
              vac      = sum(event_type == "Violence against civilians"),
              fatalities = sum(fatalities), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
    complete(TS_PCODE = ts_an$TS_PCODE, period = periods,
             fill = list(conflict = 0L, battles = 0L, erv = 0L, vac = 0L,
                         fatalities = 0)) |&gt;
    arrange(period, TS_PCODE)
}
panel_q &lt;- make_panel(conf, "yq", quarters)
stopifnot(nrow(panel_q) == nrow(ts_an) * length(quarters),
          sum(panel_q$conflict) == nrow(conf))



ACLED supplies rows only where something happened. A space-time cube needs every township in every period, and the empty cells are data: a township with no reported violence in a quarter is exactly the observation from which a cold spot is built. complete() therefore fills the full 329 × 19 grid with zeros, and two assertions check that the grid is complete and that no event was lost or double-counted in the aggregation. 31.3% of township-quarters are empty. The monthly panel (329 × 57) is built the same way, and 7 townships record no conflict event at all over the 57 months.


ACLED 只在发生了事件的地方提供记录。时空立方体需要每个镇区在每个时期都有数据,而 空单元格本身就是数据:一个季度内没有报告暴力的镇区,恰恰是构成冷点的观测。因此用 complete() 以零填满完整的 329 × 19 网格,并用两条断言检查网格是否完整、 汇总中有没有事件丢失或被重复计算。31.3% 的镇区-季度为空。月度 面板(329 × 57)以同样方式构建;有 7 个镇区在 57 个月中没有任何冲突事件。
